Install other things:
    sudo apt install nodejs npm
    node --version
    If "node --version" < 20:
        1. Install nvm
            curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.40.3/install.sh | bash
        Then reload your shell:
            source ~/.bashrc       (or simply close and open the terminal)
        2. Install Latest Node.js
            # Install latest stable version
            nvm install node
            # Or install latest LTS version
            nvm install --lts
        3. Check versions
            node --version
            npm --version
        4. Set as default for new terminals
            nvm alias default node
        5. Install AWS CDK CLI globally:
            sudo npm install -g aws-cdk
        5. Verify:
            cdk --version
        6. Create a folder inside the main folder and enter it:
            cd ~/PycharmProjects/WebsiteProject
            mkdir nova-chat-agent
            cd nova-chat-agent
        7. Install the venv package
            sudo apt install python3.12-venv
        8. Create a new project in PyCharm called CdkInfrastructure
        9. Deactivate venv in the console
            deactivate
        10.Delete everything inside the main folder
            rm -r *
            rm -r .venv
        11.Initialize the CDK Python app from the main folder:
            cdk init app --language python
        12.Activate the new environment
            source .venv/bin/activate
        13.Copy this to app.py
            import aws_cdk as cdk

            from nova_chat_agent.nova_chat_agent_stack import NovaChatAgentStack  # Import your stack

            app = cdk.App()
            NovaChatAgentStack(app, "NovaChatAgentStack",
                # Optional: Set env if not default
                env=cdk.Environment(account="322402850846", region="us-east-1"),  # Customize as needed
            )

            app.synth()
        14. Copy this to
            from aws_cdk import Stack
            from constructs import Construct
            import aws_cdk.aws_bedrock_agentcore_alpha as agentcore  # Alpha construct for AgentCore

            class NovaChatAgentStack(Stack):

                def __init__(self, scope: Construct, construct_id: str, **kwargs) -> None:
                    super().__init__(scope, construct_id, **kwargs)

                    # Your Cognito config (from your HTML)
                    user_pool_id = "eu-central-1_0MU0mOTAk"
                    identity_pool_id = "eu-central-1:c05e31b0-edb2-4190-81ed-970d7423b4f5"
                    region = "eu-central-1"

                    # Create AgentCore Runtime for Nova 2 Sonic (serverless WebSocket proxy)
                    runtime = agentcore.Runtime(self, "NovaSonicRuntime",
                        model_id="amazon.nova-2-sonic-v1:0",  # Nova 2 Sonic model
                        handler="websocket_handler.py",  # Path to your handler code (create this file next)
                        memory_enabled=True,  # For session memory
                        identity=agentcore.IdentityConfig(
                            inbound_auth=agentcore.InboundAuthConfig(
                                type="cognito",
                                user_pool_id=user_pool_id,
                                identity_pool_id=identity_pool_id
                            )
                        ),
                        websocket_config=agentcore.WebSocketConfig(
                            protocol="wss"
                        )
                    )

                    # Output the WebSocket URL for your HTML (WS_URL)
                    cdk.CfnOutput(self, "WsEndpoint", value=runtime.websocket_endpoint)

        14. Install this in the environment
            pip install \
              aws-cdk-lib==2.232.0 \
              constructs==10.3.0 \
              boto3==1.35.0 \
              aws-lambda-powertools[all]==2.43.0

        15. Run this on the terminal
            cdk synth
            sudo snap install aws-cli --classic
            aws configure
            cdk bootstrap aws://322402850846/us-east-1
            cdk deploy CdkInfrastructureStack --require-approval never

        16. Note down the web socket url and add it to the webpage:
            const WS_URL = "wss://xkl5ptgrai.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/prod";

        17. If you want to close the socket:
            cdk destroy